[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip Simple Port Cluster Bootstrap Surface\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver epic VFDhlRjOf so Port exposes one canonical cluster operator surface that can create, start, inspect, and return kubeconfig for a healthy single-node local K3s cluster without requiring operators to orchestrate raw `machine`, `guest exec`, join-token, or API-forward steps manually. (\u001b[2mVFDhlRjOf\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Move K3s bootstrap under Port ownership by making guest networking, offline artifact staging, and kubeconfig retrieval explicit Port responsibilities instead of infra-side glue or guest-side `curl get.k3s.io` scripts. (\u001b[2minspect the Port CLI/docs and confirm the blessed workflow does not depend on ad hoc in-guest install commands from another repo\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - Keep the operator contract as simple as or simpler than Slicer's K3s workflow, with single-node local as the first clean lane and multi-node or AWS expansion modeled as explicit follow-on work. (\u001b[2mreview `port --help`, cluster-facing help, and operator docs against the documented first-path experience\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFDhlRjOf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Ship Cluster-First Bootstrap UX (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-28T19:40:00Z\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFDhGw9vE/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship Simple Port Cluster Bootstrap Surface - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver epic VFDhlRjOf so Port exposes one canonical cluster operator surface that can create, start, inspect, and return kubeconfig for a healthy single-node local K3s cluster without requiring operators to orchestrate raw `machine`, `guest exec`, join-token, or API-forward steps manually. | board: VFDhlRjOf |\r\n| MG-02 | Move K3s bootstrap under Port ownership by making guest networking, offline artifact staging, and kubeconfig retrieval explicit Port responsibilities instead of infra-side glue or guest-side `curl get.k3s.io` scripts. | manual: inspect the Port CLI/docs and confirm the blessed workflow does not depend on ad hoc in-guest install commands from another repo |\r\n| MG-03 | Keep the operator contract as simple as or simpler than Slicer's K3s workflow, with single-node local as the first clean lane and multi-node or AWS expansion modeled as explicit follow-on work. | manual: review `port --help`, cluster-facing help, and operator docs against the documented first-path experience |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- The first shipped contract must be cluster-oriented, not a longer wrapper\r\n  around `port guest exec`.\r\n- Single-node local is the first success criterion. Do not require a second VM\r\n  or inter-node networking before Port can produce one healthy K3s cluster.\r\n- Avoid guest-side network fetches during bootstrap. Port should own artifact\r\n  staging and installation inputs.\r\n- Keep multi-node, AWS, and richer cluster topology explicit follow-on scope\r\n  unless they are required to make the first operator contract coherent.\r\n- Preserve the canonical Port vocabulary and keep the resulting UX simpler than\r\n  the current hosted-K3s proof path documented today.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when Port exposes one healthy local cluster contract with a usable\r\n  kubeconfig and only manual operator verification remains\r\n- YIELD to human when progress depends on product decisions about the final\r\n  cluster command vocabulary, provider naming, or which multi-node and AWS\r\n  behaviors belong in the first public contract\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFDhlRjOf\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mShip Cluster-First Bootstrap UX\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-28 19:36:58\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-28 20:42:11\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 08:35:29\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-29 08:35:29\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m11h 53m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFDhlRjOf/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFDhlRjOf/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port's current K3s workflow is still a low-level choreography:\r\n  ...\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Expose one canonical cluster-first Port surface for a healthy single-node local K3s cluster. (A named local cluster can be brought up, inspected, and torn down through a cluster-oriented \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m workflow without manual \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mguest exec\u001b[0m, join-token, or API-forward steps. -> First local cluster slice complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Move bootstrap ownership under Port instead of infra-side glue or guest-side live network fetches. (The canonical workflow stages K3s inputs through Port-owned artifacts or guest-profile inputs and does not rely on \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcurl https://get.k3s.io\u001b[0m inside the guest. -> First local cluster slice complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Make the downstream infra seam thin and explicit. (The blessed handoff reduces to \"ask Port for a healthy cluster and kubeconfig\", with raw daemon or guest choreography removed from the operator contract. -> Operator docs and proof path updated)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Keep the first cluster slice honest about what follows later. (Docs, help, and validation make single-node local the first lane while modeling multi-node, AWS, and richer guest networking as explicit follow-on work. -> Planning artifacts and proof publish the boundary clearly)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must expose a cluster-oriented operator surface for one named local K3s cluster so operators no longer assemble raw \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mguest exec\u001b[0m, join-token, or API-forward steps manually.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must make single-node local the first healthy cluster lane and fail fast on unsupported multi-node, hosted, or AWS requests in this epic. (uncovered)\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must own bootstrap inputs for the first lane through artifact-driven staging, guest-profile preparation, or equivalent Port-managed installation inputs, and the canonical workflow must not use guest-side \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcurl https://get.k3s.io\u001b[0m.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must return a usable kubeconfig and cluster health through the cluster surface without requiring manual API forwarding or kubeconfig rewriting outside Port.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Port must publish the thin infra handoff and first-slice boundaries through operator docs, help surfaces, and proof artifacts.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The new cluster surface must preserve existing \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mguest\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mservice\u001b[0m, and hosted-K3s primitives as implementation substrate without silent regressions.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Verification for the first slice must remain repo-local and reviewable through tests, CLI proofs, and at least one human-reviewable artifact.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Cluster health, ownership, and boundary output must remain explicit enough that downstream infra can tell whether a failure belongs to Port's cluster contract or to later GitOps/bootstrap work.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Prove cluster contract, local bootstrap, kubeconfig, and health behavior\r\n    - Publish the blessed local cluster workflow through docs and help surfaces,\r\n    - Validate that the canonical workflow and operator docs no longer use\r\n    - guest-side \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcurl https://get.k3s.io\u001b[0m or downstream infra choreography.\r\n    - then record one human-reviewable proof artifact through the Keel proof system.\r\n    - through story-level Rust tests and CLI command proofs.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 4 | manual 12\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 2 | manual 6\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 8 | media 1 | other 1\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFDk8fdnG\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Plan Single-Node Local Cluster Surface (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
